<title>BELGIUM: Italy concerned about EU rice import concessions.</title>
<headline>Italy concerned about EU rice import concessions.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy complained about trade concessions being considered by the European Union on imports of rice from developing countries, an EU official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Italian Farm Minister Michele Pinto expressed serious concern about the impact of such action on EU farmers at a meeting of farm ministers on Tuesday.</p>
<p>EU Farm Commissioner Franz Fischler responded that the EU pledged some trade benefits to developing countries at a World Trade Organisation conference in Singapore last year.</p>
<p>But care must be taken to avoid undermining the EU's Common Agricultural Policy (CAP), which gives preference to EU farmers, he added.</p>
<p>The European Commission was trying to balance the interests of the different interests involved, he said.</p>
</text>
